Error: Jet.MissingDisplay: Shared<Int> has no `Display` implementation
  --> Tests/UI/E0915_names_a_type_without_display_once.jet:6:27
    |
  6 |     print("couldn't read {count}")
    |                           ^^^^^
 Why: Bare `{value}` interpolation calls `Display` — there is no default for user types
 Fix: Show a part of `count` that has `Display`, or write the text yourself instead of interpolating it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.MissingDisplay
